From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:43:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] hw/input/tsc2100: Refuse a register address out of
 range on load

A frame's register address picks one of the 64 registers in a page and
is used before it is masked, so one loaded from a migration stream must
be below 64.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B1fN5Fc77Z6fVVe4rWJxPT
---
 hw/input/tsc2100.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/input/tsc2100.c b/hw/input/tsc2100.c
index a7010db55..58eb62a26 100644
--- a/hw/input/tsc2100.c
+++ b/hw/input/tsc2100.c
@@ -561,6 +561,10 @@ static int tsc2100_post_load(void *opaque, int version_id)
 {
     TSC2100State *s = opaque;
 
+    /* The register a frame is at, within its page */
+    if (s->addr >= 64) {
+        return -EINVAL;
+    }
     /* Reopen the audio voices and restart the link's clock. */
     s->rate = 0;
     tsc2100_audio_update(s);
